From 525003837eb93e1e251c6fdccedf59a5af9bbfa1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Loukious <24696530+Loukious@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:24:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] wlan: convert monitor-open QDF status to Linux errno

hdd_enable_monitor_mode() returned the raw QDF_STATUS from
cdp_set_monitor_mode() as its int result, so a non-success status reached
user space as a wrong (often positive) errno. Convert it with
qdf_status_to_os_return().

Hunk (c) of Loukious 71e6f9a; the other two hunks belong to the STA/monitor
coexistence series and do not apply to this tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_rx_monitor.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_rx_monitor.c b/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_rx_monitor.c
index 056d09f..c7643df 100644
--- a/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_rx_monitor.c
+++ b/qcacld-3.0/core/hdd/src/wlan_hdd_rx_monitor.c
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ int hdd_enable_monitor_mode(struct net_device *dev)
 	if (vdev_id == (uint8_t)-EINVAL)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	return cdp_set_monitor_mode(soc, vdev_id, false);
+	return qdf_status_to_os_return(cdp_set_monitor_mode(soc, vdev_id, false));
 }
 
 int hdd_disable_monitor_mode(void)
